         ("In the accident experiment, what effect did the word «smashed» have?", "It led to higher speed estimates and false details.", ["It made participants forget the film.", "It made participants refuse to answer.", "It led to lower speed estimates.", "It had no measurable effect."]),
         ("Why is the broken glass significant?", "There was none in the film, so it was a false memory.", ["It proved the cars were going very fast.", "It showed the film was of poor quality.", "It was the cause of the accident.", "It was mentioned in the question."]),
         ("The word «quietly» in paragraph 2 suggests that the change in memory was ___.", "subtle and unnoticed", ["loud and obvious", "deliberate and planned", "temporary and harmless", "rare and unusual"]),
         ("According to paragraph 3, false memories were more likely when ___.", "the suggestion came from a trusted family member", ["the event happened recently", "participants were very young", "the participants were police officers", "the event was described in writing"]),
         ("Why are these findings important for the legal system?", "Courts have relied heavily on confident eyewitnesses.", ["Judges never listen to witnesses.", "Police officers have poor memories.", "Witnesses are usually paid.", "Laws are written from memory."]),
         ("What change have many police forces made?", "They avoid leading questions in interviews.", ["They no longer interview witnesses.", "They only use video evidence.", "They ask witnesses to describe films.", "They interview witnesses with family members."]),
